A||||6||KnightRyder31||Lumina Engine Swap?||||1||
Z||000000||KnightRyder31||03-24-2001||10:53 AM||||Looks like the problem is pretty severe.<BR>Rod knock, spun barring...something like that.<BR>My step-dad thinks that it would be better to just replace the engine.<BR>I want a bigger engine, but he says that it would be to big of a Bi%ch to do. <BR>I thought that some lumina's came with the 3.4(Lumina Z36?), so wouldn't a 3.4 be a possible replacement? BTW I have a 3.1 in there right now.<BR>Any suggestions would be great, thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||p4n1c||03-24-2001||11:03 AM||||92 Lumina Z34 comes with the 3.4l 210hp DOHC and a 5-spd manual.<P>Actually you should be able to also get a 3.4l DOHC out of a 92 Cutlass Supreme International, both are W-Bodies.  The 92 CSI also comes stock with the 3.4l 210hp DOHC engine and a 5-spd manual.  But for both you'll probably see a lot of 4-spd autos.<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>"Each passing day, every passing face seems like such a blur" <BR>- The Offspring(Million Miles Away)||||reg||1
Z||000002||KnightRyder31||03-24-2001||09:14 PM||||Well, how hard would it be to install a new engine(3.4), and what would I need?<BR>How much money would it cost total?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||03-25-2001||06:23 PM||||There would be some(lots?) of re-wiring to put in a 3.4 TDC.  It would probably be easier to either get another 3.1 or get a 3.4 out of a newer FWD car.  Just like the Fiero, any 60* v6 will bolt right up to the tranny and fit in there.||||reg||1
Z||000004||KnightRyder31||03-26-2001||08:37 AM||||Well I could get a 3.4 out of a Lumina Z34.<BR>And that is FWD, would that make any diff?<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||03-26-2001||02:27 PM||||The Z-34 engine <I>is</I> the TDC. Major rewiring issues. <BR>The easiest swap for you is probably going to be a 3.1 from another Lumina, Grand Prix, Regal, or similar. Cavalier, Grand Am, and similar should fit too, but I'm guessing that the accessories will be more likely to be different. Some of these cars also were available with the "pushrod" 3.4. Whatever size you get, be sure to get the aluminum head DIS version. Better chance of it matching up to your ECM. <BR>(Sorry about the mis-diagnosis I gave you in the earlier thread. Obviously I couldn't hear all the knocking.)     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 03-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||KnightRyder31||03-26-2001||10:35 PM||||Well, I'm still not for sure about whats wrong with the engine. I'm guessing that it is a rod knock or spun bearing.<BR>But I'm still not for sure.||||reg||1
